  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (0.591 RNA-only vs 0.208 image-only), and the current best configuration (config_019, acc=0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder. We have zero data on alternative RNA encoders (scvi_n200, scgpt), making this the largest unexplored design axis. Question: Does a learned biological embedding (scvi_n200) outperform a linear PCA projection in the multimodal setting where RNA carries most of the signal? This experiment tests scvi_n200 in the exact best-known multimodal scaffold (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted), isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding all other factors at their empirically best values. Rationale: Since RNA drives most of the predictive signal, the encoder choice is a first-order design decision. A positive result would open a high-impact improvement direction; a null or negative result would efficiently rule out that axis. This is more informative than testing transformer aggregation (already strongly disfavored by the 7-point RNA-only gap) or re-testing image encoders (near-tie between resnet50 and ViT-L)."
}

